<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Critical Colleague – AI Use Check (Prototype)</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg:#f6f5f2; --card:#fff; --ink:#1d1d1f; --muted:#62626a; --line:#e2e0da;
    --accent:#2f4b7c; --low:#2e7d4f; --mod:#b58100; --high:#c4511f; --crit:#a3132b;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);line-height:1.5}
  main{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px 64px}
  header h1{font-size:1.6rem;margin:0 0 4px}
  header p{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}
  .tabs{display:flex;gap:8px;margin:20px 0;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .tab{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--card);padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer;font:inherit}
  .tab.active{background:var(--accent);color:#fff;border-color:var(--accent)}
  .card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:16px}
  h2{font-size:1.15rem;margin:0 0 12px}
  label{font-weight:600;display:block;margin:12px 0 6px}
  textarea,select,input[type="text"],input[type="password"]{width:100%;font:inherit;padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:#fff}
  textarea{min-height:110px;resize:vertical}
  .hint{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:4px}
  button.primary{background:var(--accent);color:#fff;border:0;padding:11px 18px;border-radius:8px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;margin-top:16px}
  button.ghost{background:none;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:9px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:inherit;cursor:pointer;margin-top:16px;margin-right:8px}
  button:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:not-allowed}
  .progress{height:6px;background:var(--line);border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:16px}
  .progress div{height:100%;background:var(--accent);transition:width .3s}
  .qnum{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em}
  .question{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;margin:4px 0 6px}
  .context{background:#eef2f8;border-left:3px solid var(--accent);padding:8px 12px;border-radius:4px;font-size:.92rem;margin:8px 0}
  .opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0;cursor:pointer;font-weight:400}
  .opt:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}
  .opt input{margin-top:4px}
  .pushback{display:none;background:#fff7e8;border-left:3px solid var(--mod);padding:10px 12px;border-radius:4px;margin-top:12px;font-size:.95rem}
  .pushback b{display:block;margin-bottom:2px}
  .rating{text-align:center;padding:18px;border-radius:10px;color:#fff;margin-bottom:16px}
  .rating .lvl{font-size:1.8rem;font-weight:700}
  .bar-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:120px 1fr 32px;gap:10px;align-items:center;margin:8px 0;font-size:.95rem}
  .bar{height:10px;background:var(--line);border-radius:5px;overflow:hidden}
  .bar div{height:100%}
  ul{padding-left:20px}
  li{margin:6px 0}
  pre{white-space:pre-wrap;background:#f1f0ec;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:14px;font-size:.85rem;max-height:420px;overflow:auto}
  .flag{color:var(--crit);font-weight:600}
  .fb-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}
  @media(max-width:560px){.fb-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  .status-msg{margin-top:12px;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;font-size:.92rem;display:none}
  .status-ok{display:block;background:#e8f5ee;border-left:3px solid var(--low);color:#1b4d30}
  .status-err{display:block;background:#fdecea;border-left:3px solid var(--crit);color:#7a0e20}
  details.gh-cfg{margin-top:14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;background:#faf9f7}
  details.gh-cfg summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)}
  footer{margin-top:32px;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted);text-align:center}
  .hidden{display:none}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <header>
    <h1>Critical Colleague</h1>
    <p>Describe how you plan to use AI. Get five tough questions, honest pushback, and a risk rating. No login, no data leaves your browser.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="tabs">
    <button class="tab active" data-tab="check">Run a check</button>
    <button class="tab" data-tab="prompt">System prompt (custom GPT)</button>
    <button class="tab" data-tab="about">About this prototype</button>
  </div>

  <!-- CHECK -->
  <section id="tab-check">
    <div class="card" id="step-intro">
      <h2>1 · Your plan</h2>
      <label for="plan">What task, and how will AI be used?</label>
      <textarea id="plan" placeholder="e.g. I want to paste customer complaint emails into ChatGPT to draft replies, then send them after a quick read."></textarea>
      <div class="hint">Be specific: which tool, what goes in, what comes out, where the output goes.</div>
      <label for="stakes">Where does the output end up?</label>
      <select id="stakes">
        <option value="1">Only for me (notes, brainstorming, a personal draft)</option>
        <option value="2" selected>Shared internally (colleagues, team documents)</option>
        <option value="3">External (customers, partners, public, graded submission)</option>
        <option value="4">Feeds decisions about people, money, health, or legal matters</option>
      </select>
      <button class="primary" id="start">Ask me the hard questions →</button>
    </div>

    <div class="card hidden" id="step-q">
      <div class="progress"><div id="prog"></div></div>
      <div class="qnum" id="qnum"></div>
      <div class="question" id="qtext"></div>
      <div id="qcontext"></div>
      <div id="qopts"></div>
      <div class="pushback" id="pushback"><b>Your colleague pushes back:</b><span id="pushtext"></span></div>
      <label for="reason">Your reasoning (optional)</label>
      <textarea id="reason" style="min-height:70px" placeholder="Write it down – putting it into words is half the exercise."></textarea>
      <button class="ghost" id="back">← Back</button>
      <button class="primary" id="next" disabled>Next →</button>
    </div>

    <div class="hidden" id="step-result">
      <div class="rating" id="ratingBox"><div>Overall risk</div><div class="lvl" id="ratingLvl"></div><div id="ratingSub"></div></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>Breakdown</h2><div id="bars"></div></div>
      <div class="card" id="flagsCard"><h2>Red flags</h2><ul id="flags"></ul></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>Before you go ahead</h2><ul id="actions"></ul></div>
      <div class="card"><h2>Your summary</h2><pre id="summary"></pre>
        <button class="ghost" id="copySummary">Copy summary</button>
        <button class="primary" id="restart">Check another plan</button>
      </div>

      <!-- FEEDBACK CARD -->
      <div class="card" id="feedback-card">
        <h2>Test feedback (for our prototype evaluation)</h2>
        <p class="hint">Help us improve Critical Colleague. Your feedback is saved directly to <code>feedback.csv</code> in our GitHub repository (or exported as CSV).</p>

        <div class="fb-grid">
          <div>
            <label for="fbChanged">Did this check change your AI plan?</label>
            <select id="fbChanged">
              <option value="Yes – changed my plan">Yes – I will adjust my plan</option>
              <option value="Partially – added a check">Partially – I will add a review step</option>
              <option value="No – kept plan as is">No – I will proceed as planned</option>
              <option value="Stopped – won't use AI here">Stopped – I won't use AI for this</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="fbHelp">How helpful were the questions & pushback?</label>
            <select id="fbHelp">
              <option value="5">5 – Very helpful</option>
              <option value="4" selected>4 – Helpful</option>
              <option value="3">3 – Neutral</option>
              <option value="2">2 – Not very helpful</option>
              <option value="1">1 – Not helpful at all</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>

        <label for="fbComment">What felt realistic, annoying, or missing?</label>
        <textarea id="fbComment" style="min-height:80px" placeholder="e.g. Question 2 made me realize I don't verify citations, or the rating felt too strict..."></textarea>

        <details class="gh-cfg">
          <summary>GitHub Repo Connection (saves directly to feedback.csv)</summary>
          <div class="hint" style="margin-bottom:8px">Enter your repository details once (stored locally in your browser). Never commit a Personal Access Token into public code!</div>
          <div class="fb-grid">
            <div>
              <label for="ghOwner">GitHub Owner / Username</label>
              <input type="text" id="ghOwner" placeholder="e.g. janlippinghof">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="ghRepo">Repository Name</label>
              <input type="text" id="ghRepo" placeholder="e.g. entrepreneurship">
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="fb-grid">
            <div>
              <label for="ghPath">CSV File Path in Repo</label>
              <input type="text" id="ghPath" value="feedback.csv">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="ghToken">Fine-grained GitHub Token (Contents: Read & Write)</label>
              <input type="password" id="ghToken" placeholder="github_pat_...">
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>

        <button class="primary" id="submitFb">Save feedback to GitHub (feedback.csv)</button>
        <button class="ghost" id="downloadCsv">Download CSV row locally</button>
        <div class="status-msg" id="fbStatus"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROMPT -->
  <section id="tab-prompt" class="hidden">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>System prompt for a custom GPT / Claude Project</h2>
      <p class="hint">Paste this into the instructions field. The LLM version asks follow-ups in free text and adapts to your answers; this page uses fixed questions and transparent rules instead.</p>
      <pre id="sysprompt"></pre>
      <button class="primary" id="copyPrompt">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ABOUT -->
  <section id="tab-about" class="hidden">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>How the rating works</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Each of the five dimensions is scored 0 (low risk) to 3 (high risk). "I don't know" scores 3 – not knowing is itself the risk.</li>
        <li>The total (0–15) is weighted by where the output ends up (×0.8 personal … ×1.4 decisions about people/money/health/law).</li>
        <li>Bands: under 4 Low · under 8 Moderate · under 11 High · 11+ Critical.</li>
        <li>Red-flag rules override the average, e.g. sensitive data + no reviewer is at least High, no matter how good the rest looks.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Known limits</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It rates your <em>self-reported</em> answers. Optimistic answers produce optimistic ratings.</li>
        <li>Keyword detection for context hints is crude; it can miss or over-flag.</li>
        <li>It is a thinking exercise, not a compliance or legal assessment (e.g. GDPR, EU AI Act).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>Prototype v0.1 · Created with AI assistance (Claude Opus 5.5, Anthropic) · Review before use.</footer>
</main>

<script>
const DIMENSIONS = [
  {
    key:"data", label:"Data",
    q:"What exactly goes into the tool – and would you be fine if it showed up in tomorrow's newspaper?",
    kw:[/customer|client|employee|patient|student|applicant|cv|resume|salary|personal|contract|confidential|email|health|hr/i,
        "Your description mentions content that likely contains personal or confidential data. Check whether the tool you use is approved and what it does with inputs."],
    opts:[
      ["Only public or self-written, non-sensitive content",0,"Fine – but check again in six months. Inputs tend to creep from 'harmless' to 'just this once, the real file'."],
      ["Internal information, in a company-approved tool with a data agreement",1,"Do you know what the agreement actually covers – training on your data, retention, where it's stored? 'Approved' is often assumed, not checked."],
      ["Internal or confidential information, in a tool I haven't checked",2,"Then you are making a data-protection decision on behalf of your organisation without the information to make it. Who should have made it?"],
      ["Personal data about people (customers, staff, applicants) or confidential data, in an unapproved tool",3,"This is the scenario most data-protection incidents start with. Could you anonymise the input, or use an approved tool instead?"],
      ["I don't know",3,"Not knowing what you put in is the problem. Find out before the first upload, not after."]
    ],
    fix:"Strip names and identifiers before input, or switch to an approved tool. Ask your data-protection contact one specific question: 'May I put X into tool Y?'"
  },
  {
    key:"errors", label:"Errors",
    q:"Assume the output is confidently wrong in one place. How would you notice – and what happens if you don't?",
    kw:[/number|figure|financ|legal|law|translat|code|calculat|statistic|summar|citation|source|medical|dose/i,
        "Your task involves numbers, facts, legal wording, code or summaries – areas where AI errors look plausible and are easy to miss."],
    opts:[
      ["Errors would be obvious and harmless",0,"Are you sure? The dangerous errors are the ones that look exactly like correct answers."],
      ["I'd catch them with a normal check; consequences are minor and reversible",1,"What is a 'normal check' here, concretely? If you can't name it, you won't do it under time pressure."],
      ["Errors could be subtle (facts, figures, wording) and hard to spot",2,"Then reading it once won't catch them. What source would you compare against?"],
      ["Errors would be hard to spot AND hard to undo once acted on",3,"This combination is where AI should draft at most, never decide. What's your safety net?"],
      ["I haven't thought about it",3,"Then do it now: name the single worst plausible error and its consequence."]
    ],
    fix:"Write down the worst plausible error. Define a concrete check against an independent source (original data, the law text, a test run) for exactly that error type."
  },
  {
    key:"check", label:"Who checks",
    q:"Who reviews the output before it's used – and do they know enough to disagree with it?",
    kw:[/automat|directly|straight|without|bulk|batch|all of|every/i,
        "Your description sounds like outputs may flow on with little or no human review."],
    opts:[
      ["A qualified person checks every output against sources",0,"Good. Does that person have the time – or will 'check' become 'skim' by week three?"],
      ["I check it myself, and I know the subject well",1,"Self-review of something you asked for is weak: you see what you expected. Would a second pair of eyes be cheap here?"],
      ["Spot checks or a quick skim",2,"A skim catches formatting, not fluent nonsense. Which outputs get skipped, and why those?"],
      ["No one – it goes straight out",3,"Then the AI is effectively making the final call. Is that what you intend?"]
    ],
    fix:"Name the reviewer, define what they compare against, and budget their time. If nobody qualified can review, reduce the AI's role to drafting."
  },
  {
    key:"account", label:"Accountability",
    q:"If this goes wrong, whose name is on it – and could that person explain how the result came about?",
    kw:[/decid|decision|hiring|recruit|grade|assess|evaluat|approv|reject|score/i,
        "Your task looks like it influences decisions about people or outcomes. 'The AI suggested it' will not hold up as a justification."],
    opts:[
      ["Clearly me (or a named owner), and I can explain and reproduce the reasoning",0,"Good. Can you also explain it to the person affected by it, in plain words?"],
      ["Clear owner, but they couldn't fully explain the AI's part",1,"Owning what you can't explain is a weak position. What would you say if challenged?"],
      ["Shared or unclear between people or teams",2,"Shared responsibility usually means nobody's. Who gets the call when it fails?"],
      ["Nobody specifically / 'the tool'",3,"Tools can't be accountable. Someone will be held responsible – better to decide who now."]
    ],
    fix:"Name one owner. Make sure they can explain the result without referring to the AI, or document the prompt, inputs and checks so it is reconstructible."
  },
  {
    key:"loss", label:"What you'd lose",
    q:"What would you or your team stop learning, noticing or doing by handing this to AI?",
    kw:[/learn|practi|write|analy|feedback|relationship|customer contact|thesis|assignment|essay|report/i,
        "This task may build skills or relationships. Outsourcing it can be efficient now and costly later."],
    opts:[
      ["Nothing meaningful – routine work with no learning value",0,"Plausible. But routine tasks are often where newcomers learn the ropes. Is it routine for everyone?"],
      ["Some practice, and I accept that deliberately",1,"Fine, if it stays a choice. How would you notice if the skill had faded?"],
      ["A core skill, judgment, or relationship would weaken over time",2,"Then the short-term gain has a long-term price. Could AI support the task instead of doing it?"],
      ["I haven't considered it / it would replace the point of the task",3,"If the task exists to build understanding (e.g. coursework), AI doing it defeats its purpose."]
    ],
    fix:"Decide which part stays human on purpose (e.g. first draft, the key judgment, the client conversation). Use AI for critique or the second pass instead."
  }
];

const STAKES = {1:{f:0.8,t:"personal use"},2:{f:1.0,t:"internal use"},3:{f:1.2,t:"external use"},4:{f:1.4,t:"decisions about people / money / health / law"}};
const LEVELS = [
  {max:4,name:"Low",color:"var(--low)",sub:"Reasonable plan. Keep the checks you described."},
  {max:8,name:"Moderate",color:"var(--mod)",sub:"Workable, with specific gaps to close first."},
  {max:11,name:"High",color:"var(--high)",sub:"Don't go ahead as described. Fix the flagged areas."},
  {max:99,name:"Critical",color:"var(--crit)",sub:"Stop and redesign. Involve someone responsible for data, quality or compliance."}
];

let idx=0, answers=[], reasons=[], planText="", stakes=2, lastResult=null;
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);

document.querySelectorAll(".tab").forEach(t=>t.onclick=()=>{
  document.querySelectorAll(".tab").forEach(x=>x.classList.remove("active"));
  t.classList.add("active");
  ["check","prompt","about"].forEach(n=>$("tab-"+n).classList.toggle("hidden",n!==t.dataset.tab));
});

$("start").onclick=()=>{
  planText=$("plan").value.trim();
  if(planText.length<20){alert("Describe your plan in at least a sentence – vague plans get vague answers.");return;}
  stakes=+$("stakes").value; idx=0; answers=[]; reasons=[];
  $("step-intro").classList.add("hidden"); $("step-q").classList.remove("hidden");
  renderQ();
};

function renderQ(){
  const d=DIMENSIONS[idx];
  $("prog").style.width=(idx/DIMENSIONS.length*100)+"%";
  $("qnum").textContent=`Question ${idx+1} of ${DIMENSIONS.length} · ${d.label}`;
  $("qtext").textContent=d.q;
  $("qcontext").innerHTML=d.kw[0].test(planText)?`<div class="context">${d.kw[1]}</div>`:"";
  $("qopts").innerHTML=d.opts.map((o,i)=>`<label class="opt"><input type="radio" name="opt" value="${i}" ${answers[idx]===i?"checked":""}><span>${o[0]}</span></label>`).join("");
  $("reason").value=reasons[idx]||"";
  $("back").style.visibility=idx===0?"hidden":"visible";
  $("next").textContent=idx===DIMENSIONS.length-1?"See my risk rating →":"Next →";
  showPush();
  document.querySelectorAll('input[name=opt]').forEach(r=>r.onchange=()=>{answers[idx]=+r.value;showPush();});
}
function showPush(){
  const a=answers[idx];
  $("next").disabled=a===undefined;
  $("pushback").style.display=a===undefined?"none":"block";
  if(a!==undefined) $("pushtext").textContent=DIMENSIONS[idx].opts[a][2];
}
$("next").onclick=()=>{reasons[idx]=$("reason").value.trim(); if(idx<DIMENSIONS.length-1){idx++;renderQ();}else showResult();};
$("back").onclick=()=>{reasons[idx]=$("reason").value.trim(); idx--; renderQ();};

function showResult(){
  const s=DIMENSIONS.map((d,i)=>d.opts[answers[i]][1]);
  const sc=Object.fromEntries(DIMENSIONS.map((d,i)=>[d.key,s[i]]));
  const raw=s.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  let score=raw*STAKES[stakes].f;
  let lvlIdx=LEVELS.findIndex(l=>score<l.max);
  const flags=[];
  const floor=(min,msg)=>{flags.push(msg); if(lvlIdx<min) lvlIdx=min;};
  if(sc.data===3&&sc.check>=2) floor(2,"Sensitive or unknown data combined with weak or no review.");
  if(stakes===4&&sc.check>=2) floor(2,"Output feeds decisions about people/money/health/law without solid review.");
  if(sc.errors===3&&sc.check===3) floor(2,"Hard-to-detect errors and nobody checks.");
  if(sc.account===3) floor(1,"No one is accountable for the result.");
  if(stakes===4&&sc.account>=2&&sc.data>=2) floor(3,"High-stakes decision, unclear owner, and risky data handling.");
  const dk=DIMENSIONS.filter((d,i)=>d.opts[answers[i]][0].startsWith("I don't know")||d.opts[answers[i]][0].startsWith("I haven't")).map(d=>d.label);
  if(dk.length) flags.push("You answered 'don't know / haven't thought about it' for: "+dk.join(", ")+".");
  const L=LEVELS[lvlIdx];

  lastResult = {
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    plan: planText,
    stakes: STAKES[stakes].t,
    score: score.toFixed(1),
    riskLevel: L.name,
    scores: sc,
    flagsCount: flags.length
  };

  $("step-q").classList.add("hidden"); $("step-result").classList.remove("hidden");
  $("ratingBox").style.background=L.color; $("ratingLvl").textContent=L.name;
  $("ratingSub").textContent=`${L.sub} (score ${score.toFixed(1)} · weighted for ${STAKES[stakes].t})`;
  const col=v=>["var(--low)","var(--mod)","var(--high)","var(--crit)"][v];
  $("bars").innerHTML=DIMENSIONS.map((d,i)=>`<div class="bar-row"><span>${d.label}</span><div class="bar"><div style="width:${s[i]/3*100}%;background:${col(s[i])}"></div></div><span>${s[i]}/3</span></div>`).join("");
  $("flagsCard").style.display=flags.length?"block":"none";
  $("flags").innerHTML=flags.map(f=>`<li class="flag">${f}</li>`).join("");
  const acts=DIMENSIONS.map((d,i)=>[s[i],d]).filter(x=>x[0]>=1).sort((a,b)=>b[0]-a[0]);
  $("actions").innerHTML=acts.length?acts.map(([v,d])=>`<li><b>${d.label}:</b> ${d.fix}</li>`).join(""):"<li>No gaps flagged. Re-run the check if the task, the data or the tool changes.</li>";

  $("summary").textContent=
`CRITICAL COLLEAGUE – AI USE CHECK
Plan: ${planText}
Output used for: ${STAKES[stakes].t}
Overall risk: ${L.name} (score ${score.toFixed(1)})

${DIMENSIONS.map((d,i)=>`${d.label} [${s[i]}/3]: ${d.opts[answers[i]][0]}${reasons[i]?"
  Reasoning: "+reasons[i]:""}`).join("
")}
${flags.length?"
Red flags:
- "+flags.join("
- "):""}

Self-assessment, not a compliance review. Generated with a prototype built with AI assistance (Claude Opus 5.5).`;
  $("fbStatus").className="status-msg";
  $("fbStatus").textContent="";
  $("submitFb").disabled=false;
  window.scrollTo(0,0);
}

$("restart").onclick=()=>{ $("step-result").classList.add("hidden"); $("step-intro").classList.remove("hidden"); window.scrollTo(0,0); };
function copy(text,btn){ navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(()=>{const o=btn.textContent;btn.textContent="Copied ✓";setTimeout(()=>btn.textContent=o,1500);}).catch(()=>alert("Copy failed – select the text manually.")); }
$("copySummary").onclick=e=>copy($("summary").textContent,e.target);
$("copyPrompt").onclick=e=>copy($("sysprompt").textContent,e.target);

// --- FEEDBACK & GITHUB CSV INTEGRATION ---
const CSV_HEADER = "timestamp,plan,stakes,risk_level,score,data_score,errors_score,check_score,accountability_score,loss_score,flags_count,plan_changed,helpfulness_rating,comment";

function csvEscape(val){
  const str = String(val ?? "").replace(/
?
/g, " ");
  return `"${str.replace(/"/g, '""')}"`;
}

function buildCsvRow(){
  const r = lastResult || {};
  const sc = r.scores || {};
  return [
    r.timestamp || new Date().toISOString(),
    r.plan || "",
    r.stakes || "",
    r.riskLevel || "",
    r.score || "",
    sc.data ?? "",
    sc.errors ?? "",
    sc.check ?? "",
    sc.account ?? "",
    sc.loss ?? "",
    r.flagsCount ?? "",
    $("fbChanged").value,
    $("fbHelp").value,
    $("fbComment").value.trim()
  ].map(csvEscape).join(",");
}

// Load saved GitHub settings from localStorage (and URL query params if shared for user testing)
(function initGhConfig(){
  const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
  ["owner","repo","path","token"].forEach(k=>{
    const el = $("gh" + k[0].toUpperCase() + k.slice(1));
    const saved = params.get("gh_" + k) || localStorage.getItem("cc_gh_" + k);
    if(saved) el.value = saved;
    el.addEventListener("change", ()=> localStorage.setItem("cc_gh_" + k, el.value.trim()));
  });
})();

function setFbStatus(msg, ok){
  const el = $("fbStatus");
  el.textContent = msg;
  el.className = "status-msg " + (ok ? "status-ok" : "status-err");
}

$("downloadCsv").onclick=()=>{
  const content = CSV_HEADER + "
" + buildCsvRow() + "
";
  const blob = new Blob([content], {type:"text/csv;charset=utf-8;"});
  const a = document.createElement("a");
  a.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  a.download = `critical-colleague-feedback-${new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10)}.csv`;
  a.click();
};

$("submitFb").onclick=async ()=>{
  const owner = $("ghOwner").value.trim();
  const repo = $("ghRepo").value.trim();
  const path = $("ghPath").value.trim() || "feedback.csv";
  const token = $("ghToken").value.trim();

  if(!owner || !repo || !token){
    document.querySelector("details.gh-cfg").open = true;
    setFbStatus("Please fill in GitHub Owner, Repository Name, and Token in the 'GitHub Repo Connection' section above (or use 'Download CSV row locally').", false);
    return;
  }

  localStorage.setItem("cc_gh_owner", owner);
  localStorage.setItem("cc_gh_repo", repo);
  localStorage.setItem("cc_gh_path", path);
  localStorage.setItem("cc_gh_token", token);

  const btn = $("submitFb");
  btn.disabled = true;
  btn.textContent = "Saving to GitHub...";

  const apiUrl = `https://api.github.com/repos/${encodeURIComponent(owner)}/${encodeURIComponent(repo)}/contents/${path.split("/").map(encodeURIComponent).join("/")}`;
  const headers = {
    "Authorization": `Bearer ${token}`,
    "Accept": "application/vnd.github+json",
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
  };

  try {
    let existingContent = "";
    let sha = null;

    const getRes = await fetch(apiUrl, {headers});
    if(getRes.ok){
      const fileData = await getRes.json();
      sha = fileData.sha;
      const binStr = atob(fileData.content.replace(/
/g, ""));
      const bytes = Uint8Array.from(binStr, c => c.charCodeAt(0));
      existingContent = new TextDecoder().decode(bytes);
    } else if(getRes.status !== 404){
      const err = await getRes.json().catch(()=>({}));
      throw new Error(err.message || `GitHub GET failed (${getRes.status})`);
    }

    const row = buildCsvRow();
    let updatedCsv = existingContent.trim()
      ? existingContent.trimEnd() + "
" + row + "
"
      : CSV_HEADER + "
" + row + "
";

    const utf8Bytes = new TextEncoder().encode(updatedCsv);
    let bin = "";
    utf8Bytes.forEach(b => bin += String.fromCharCode(b));
    const encodedContent = btoa(bin);

    const body = {
      message: `Add test feedback (${new Date().toISOString().slice(0,16)})`,
      content: encodedContent
    };
    if(sha) body.sha = sha;

    const putRes = await fetch(apiUrl, {
      method: "PUT",
      headers,
      body: JSON.stringify(body)
    });

    if(!putRes.ok){
      const err = await putRes.json().catch(()=>({}));
      throw new Error(err.message || `GitHub PUT failed (${putRes.status})`);
    }

    setFbStatus(`Saved! Feedback appended to ${owner}/${repo}/${path}.`, true);
    btn.textContent = "Feedback saved ✓";
  } catch(e){
    setFbStatus("Could not save to GitHub: " + e.message, false);
    btn.disabled = false;
    btn.textContent = "Save feedback to GitHub (feedback.csv)";
  }
};

$("sysprompt").textContent=
`ROLE
You are "Critical Colleague": an experienced, sceptical but friendly co-worker. The user describes how they plan to use AI for a task. Your job is to make them think critically before they start. You are not a compliance officer and you never shame anyone. You are direct, specific, and brief.

PROCESS
1. If the description is vague (no tool, no inputs, no destination of output), ask ONE clarifying question first.
2. Ask exactly five tough questions, ONE AT A TIME. Wait for the answer before the next. Tailor each to the user's specific plan; never ask generically.
   Q1 Data – What exactly goes into the tool? Personal, confidential, or third-party data? Is the tool approved?
   Q2 Errors – Assume the output is confidently wrong in one place. How would they notice? What happens if they don't?
   Q3 Who checks – Who reviews before use, against what, and are they competent to disagree?
   Q4 Accountability – Whose name is on the result? Could they explain it without saying "the AI said so"?
   Q5 What you'd lose – Which skill, judgment, learning or relationship erodes if AI does this?
3. After each answer, give ONE short pushback sentence if the answer is vague, optimistic or assumes something unchecked. If the answer is solid, say so in a few words and move on. Treat "I don't know" as a high-risk answer, without judgment.
4. After Q5, give the assessment.

SCORING
Score each dimension 0 (low risk) to 3 (high risk). Weight the total by stakes: personal ×0.8, internal ×1.0, external ×1.2, decisions about people/money/health/law ×1.4.
Bands: <4 Low, <8 Moderate, <11 High, ≥11 Critical.
Overrides (minimum level regardless of score):
- Sensitive/unknown data AND weak or no review → at least High.
- High-stakes decisions AND weak review → at least High.
- No accountable person → at least Moderate.

OUTPUT FORMAT (after Q5)
- Overall risk: [Level] – one-sentence reason.
- Table: Dimension | Score 0–3 | Why (max 12 words).
- Red flags (if any).
- Top 3 concrete actions before starting, most important first.
- One question the user should ask someone else (e.g. data-protection contact, supervisor).

RULES
- Never do the task itself. Only assess the plan.
- Don't lecture, moralise or use motivational language.
- Don't invent laws or policies. If regulation may apply (e.g. GDPR, EU AI Act, company policy), say "check with [role]" rather than giving legal conclusions.
- Remind the user once, at the start, not to paste real confidential data into this chat – describing it is enough.
- Language: reply in the user's language.`;
</script>
